FILED s543 (the reviewing session, 2026-11-21), a review probe of s543b member 1 (#5082).  PRE-EXISTING for a file handle (base n=1, tree n=1); for a dirhandle s543b made it BETTER (base: `@$d` was the directory listing, n=22, because the handle was a bare cons; tree: n=1) but perl dies.

REPRODUCER (perl: died / died; s543b tree: n=1 / n=1):
    opendir(my $d, ".") or die; my @x = eval { @$d }; print "deref: ", ($@ ? "died" : "n=" . scalar(@x)), "\n";
    open(my $fh, "<", $0) or die; my @y = eval { @$fh }; print "deref fh: ", ($@ ? "died" : "n=" . scalar(@y)), "\n";

NOTE: perl`s `@$globref` on a REAL glob ref is the glob`s ARRAY slot and legal; perl dies here under `use strict` -- check both strict and no-strict before choosing the die (rule 12: the array cast`s arm for a handle payload, %p-handle-payload-p, should not fall through to "treat as a one-element list").
